ment","name":"Small and Midsize Business (SMB)","description":"Small and Midsize Business (SMB)","dateCreated":"2021-06-04T06:35:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:15+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#wynkmusic","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"wynkmusic","dateCreated":"2021-06-18T07:37:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2021-12-22T23:24:45+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"Wynk Music reduces computing costs by 60 percent and simplifies analytics by running its big data framework on AWS. As part of Bharti Airtel Limited’s digital portfolio in India, Wynk Music is an audio streaming app and website with 72 million monthly active users. The company uses Amazon EMR as its big data platform, Amazon EC2 Spot Instances to control costs, and Amazon Redshift as a data warehouse.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/apac/customer-references-logos-(@1x---@2x)/Wynk_logo@1x.3ff1ed171fdd0f3dd986f6e2bb9bdfa2042346fc.png","displayLocation":"India","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Media \u0026 Entertainment","sortDate":"2021-06-17","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/wynkmusic/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2021","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Wynk Slashes Compute Costs for Big Data by 60% with Amazon EMR and Spot Instances","customer-name":"Wynk Music"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#product#redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Redshift","description":"Amazon Redshift","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:05:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:56+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#cost-mgmt","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Cost Management","description":"Cost Management","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-03-05T03:54:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#customer-enablement#business-support","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#customer-enableme